    {
      "text": "Probing the singularity at the holographic screen via q-holography — We study the emergence of q-deformed spacetime in a lower-dimensional gravitational system whose asymptotic region geometrizes the\n\n**Probing the singularity at the holographic screen via q-holography**\n\n*Department of Physics and Astronomy*\n\n44 pp, 14 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We study the emergence of q-deformed spacetime in a lower-dimensional gravitational system whose asymptotic region geometrizes the global symmetry of a q-deformed CFT. More precisely, we consider the 2d sinh dilaton gravity model, whose classical metric solutions exhibit a curvature singularity at the holographic boundary. Our aim is to probe this UV near-boundary regime by injecting a small probe into the bulk, and identifying the geometrical features it observes. At the level of the two- point correlator, we see the emergence of q-deformed hyperbolic disk isometries. By formulating DSSYK in terms of the analogous sine dilaton gravity model, we expect this q-deformed holographic duality to persist. July 21, 2025 ∗andreas.belaey@ugent.be †thomas.mertens@ugent.be ‡jacopo.papalini@ugent.be arXiv:2507.13873v1 [hep-th] 18 Jul 2025\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Correlation functions on the quantum disk; q-Correlation functions; Quantum hyperbolic disk; A candidate bulk description for q-holography; Definition and classical structure of sinh dil; Probe regime of sinh dilaton gravity; Concluding remarks; Corepresentations of (quasi)-primary operators; Dilaton gravity models; Holographic counterterm; Sinh dilaton gravity quantization; Useful manipulations involving Ramanujan's for",
